<title>UK: Algeria raises June LPG by $10 to $175/$180 a tonn.</title>
<headline>Algeria raises June LPG by $10 to $175/$180 a tonn.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach has raised its official posted prices for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) for June.</p>
<p>Propane will be $175 a tonne fob Bethioua, an increase of $10 a tonne from May.</p>
<p>Butane will be $180 a tonne for Bethioua, also a rise of $10 a tonne from the previous month.</p>
<p>The premium for loading at Arzew or Skikda has been set at $5 a tonne.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
